  "name": "Ópera flamenca (1920s-1950s staged flamenco)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ópera flamenca was the name under which flamenco toured theatres and bullrings from the mid-1920s to the 1950s, reportedly adopted because opera performances paid less tax than variety shows. Its stars — Pepe Marchena, Manuel Vallejo, La Niña de la Puebla and later Juanito Valderrama — favoured the lighter, melodic cantes, above all personal fandangos, colombianas, guajiras, milongas and cuplés por bulerías, and recorded them prolifically on 78-rpm discs and EPs.",
